    "answer": {
      "short": "$5\\text{ m}$. Use $2\\pi r^2+2\\pi r(r+4)=140\\pi$ and take the positive root.",
      "worked": "Let $r$ be the radius in metres. Then $h=r+4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}SA&=2\\pi r^2+2\\pi rh\\\\140\\pi&=2\\pi r^2+2\\pi r(r+4)\\\\140\\pi&=4\\pi r^2+8\\pi r\\\\r^2+2r-35&=0\\\\(r+7)(r-5)&=0\\\\r&=-7\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $r>0$, the radius is $5\\text{ m}$ and the height is $9\\text{ m}$.\n\nCheck: $2\\pi(5)^2+2\\pi(5)(9)=140\\pi\\text{ m}^2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
